                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><table style="border-collapse: collapse; border-color: #ccc;  border: 1px solid #000000;" border="1">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem; border: 1px solid #000000;" width="908">
<p>Through practice and other ways, share the humanistic stories in stomatology with the&nbsp;students, guide them to experience the basic concepts of Stomatology, the concept of life-cycle health, tertiary prevention of oral diseases, self-oral health care and oral health education. The objective of the course is to instill the idea of "prevention first" as early as possible to the students, changing from "disease-centered" to "health-centered", from "individual-centered" to "people-centered", and to cultivate high quality students of Stomatology for the new era.</p>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
